// TEST: Range SymIdx Tagged Slot Warns
// The tag side of `range<SymIdx<...>>`, and the one spelling of the three that
// still warns -- deliberately.
//
// `range<LatIdx>` flows LatIdx's tag onto the kernel's index param, which is
// what makes `A(i)` typecheck with no annotation
// (TypeCheck.elemTypeForIterationIndex). The group here is anonymous on BOTH
// counts -- no alias AND a literal extent -- so there is no component tag
// anywhere to inherit: the params come out plain Int64, every read of the
// I3-tagged array `v` is an untagged-integer index, and that is BL4003 as a
// WARNING, twice (v(p0) and v(p0 + p1)). The program compiles and runs to
// 172's values.
//
// This file is the CONTROL for the other two spellings, which both name the
// component space somewhere and are now both silent:
//   - `range<SymIdx<2, I3>>` names the component inline -- the base slot
//     resolves to I3's record and inherits its tag (index-types/239).
//   - `range<S2>` for `type S2 = SymIdx<2, I3>` names the group -- a
//     multi-rank record now keeps its COMPONENT tag rather than having it
//     overwritten by the alias name (175, which used to be this file's
//     hard-ERROR twin and is now its silent one).
// Writing the extent literally, as here, is what opts out of the tag
// discipline -- so this warning is the discipline working, not a gap.
// See docs/formalism.md 7.3.
type I3 = Idx<3>
let v: Array<Float like I3> = [2.0, 3.0, 5.0]
let sym = method_for(range<SymIdx<2, 3>>) <@> lambda(p0, p1) -> v(p0) * v(p0 + p1) |> compute
// WARN: BL4003  (untagged index into an I3-tagged slot)
// EXPECT: sym = [[4, 6, 10], [9, 15], [25]]
